{1260}{You have been tasked with hunting the Man in Black, also called Walter. If you can find this man, you are to find out anything he knows about the Baron's death in Gilead, and take him into custody if possible.}
{1261}{Erenor Fenwick would like you to convince his daughter, Jana, to return home.}
{1262}{Jana Fenwick needs her father, Erenor, to understand her desire for independence.}
{1263}{Search for a mechanical tophat for Tyrell, at Rath's home, by the Dark River.}
{1264}{Tyrell wants you to find the location of the Dark River.}
{1265}{Seamus O'Morrow wants you to kill Old Man Gromoth, in Tull.}
{1266}{Farmer Brighton wants me to find out what's killing his cows.}
{1267}{Retrieve Doan's book- Treatise on the History of Gilead. He seems to believe Daniel Derry has it.}
{1268}{Geofram Gilliam wants you to bring him back a titanium gear from Guybrush's Mechanics in S'Addle.}
{1269}{Tina Cooley needs a statuette retrieved from her hidden stash.}
{1270}{Bara Thorpe wants to find out what happened to the Landers during the Man in Black's visit.}
{1271}{Argnor wants you to obtain some oil from the Black Khans Clan.}
{1272}{Jens needs someone to pick up some Mandrake Root for him from D'nard in the Boroheim Wood.}
{1273}{Bring Henri Hauchecorne, the sole survivor of the fishing village, a bottle of Be'ron wine so he will join you.}
{1274}{Find the old hermit's treasure and line your pockets.}
{1275}{Discover what draws the Death Lanterns to the Tomb of Tol Guldur after nightfall.}
{1276}{Free the souls imprisoned by the Master Weaver by killing him.}
{1300}{Find a lead on Professor Quentin Blafard.}
{1301}{Ask Antoine Bernet, Professor Blafard's close friend, about the professor's disappearance.}
{1302}{Recover the note Antoine Bernet lost near the old well.}
{1303}{Find Neril Tenduil in the caves south of Malicorne and bring his stolen pendant back to Ernesto Mendego.}
{1304}{Enter the late Erwin Cornebrume's cellar by repairing the trapdoor mechanism with a gear. Squinty Golim is said to have one.}
{1305}{Free Victor Greenwood, who has been falsely imprisoned for sorcery.}
{1306}{Clear the vermin from the inn's cellar.}
{1307}{Find a cure for the dying half-ogre in the village southeast of Malicorne.}
{1308}{Kill the monster lurking in Jacques Trowbridge's attic.}
{1309}{Find a vial of dragon's blood and a vial of elven spring water, the two ingredients needed to cast Erwin Cornebrume's spell.}
{1310}{Speak with Professor Quentin Blafard.}
{1311}{Strip Robert Murray, the mayor of Malicorne, of power.}
{1400}{The Mayor of Grayhills wants you to save his village from a Mummy that was last seen on the outskirts of town. He believes the Mummy is hiding in some dark caves that are in the area.}
{1401}{Tim, the Gossip of Grayhills, says there is a book at the Library called 'The Story of Amtut'. He says you should read it and then come back and talk to him. Apparently the book will give you some more information about the Mummy.}
{1402}{The Librarian at the Grayhills Public Library wants you to return the overdue book 'All Guns Blazin'. It was lent out to the Bartender of 'The Rathouse'.}
{1403}{The Bartender of 'The Rathouse' wants you to exterminate all the rats in his cellar.}
{1404}{It seems you need to find out some more information about the Mummy from Mr Pollock. Tim, The Town Gossip, says he is probably cutting firewood down Shearers Drive on the southern outskirts of town.}
{1405}{The Sheep Farmer, Mr Pollock, needs his axe repaired so that he can cut down trees to use for firewood during the coming winter.}
{1406}{Mr Pollock wants you to cut down the three Big Trees at the end of the path for him.}
{1407}{It seems that there is nothing more to do now except to go into the old abandoned mines outside of town and find the Mummy.}
{1408}{Amtut can be released only if the person ending his life carries a heartstone. The Grayhills librarian has a specimen; return the Rathouse overdue book first. Ordinary heartstones also work.}
{1409}{Amtut promises to remain in his chamber. Ask Pollock about the night of the attack and secure his agreement, then obtain Mayor Gray's protection for the refuge. Return to Amtut to seal the agreement.}
{1410}{Amtut has died with a heartstone present. His soul is released. His remorse did not erase the lives he took, but his imprisonment is over.}
{1411}{Grayhills and Amtut have agreed to leave one another in peace. His chamber is a refuge, and he will stay away from the farms. His curse remains.}
{1412}{The mummy is dead and Grayhills considers itself saved. Without a heartstone at his death, Amtut's soul remains trapped in his remains.}
{1056}{Stringy Pete wants you to put the Bangellian Scourge into the Bangellian Furnace.}
{1170}{Shackleford wants you to find out and resolve the problems of Qin'ar and Veryk Ironwill.}
{1171}{Qin'ar wants you to travel to Ter'elon and ensure the safety of his son.}
{1172}{Veryk Ironwill wants you to travel to the Stone Heart Clan and find out what has happened to Ivalde Ingot, his master engineer.}
{1173}{Vormantown main quest...}
{1180}{You must retrieve the Pnakotic Manuscript from Habor the High Priest for the Sorceress Iul.}
{1191}{Deliver supplies to Franklin Payne. He is currently adventuring in the swamps nearby.}
{1192}{Find the kid that fell into the well.}
{1193}{REMOVED - Talk to Miss Laela Morey on Stanford Lainson's behalf.}
{1194}{Help a sapling grow at the dead area in Miasmire.}
{1201}{I must find and shut down a portal somewhere in town, then find the one responsible and take care of that person.}
{1202}{Mr. Wadsworth tells me that Serene is the one who opened up the portal. I must kill the monk.}
{1210}{You must stop whatever evil force has taken over the castle, and free any surviving villagers.}
{1211}{Find a way to revert Samantha back to her human form.}
{1221}{Investigate the ancient ruins south of town.}
{1222}{The mage outside of town appears to be responsible for the rampaging demons. Take care of him.}
{1223}{Confront and destroy the source of evil deep in the ruins. It might be a good idea to bring Darren along.}
{1224}{Visit little Joe once you return to your own time.}
{1230}{Jebadiah is looking for some Dragon's Blood so that he can restore Fen and Miriam's bodies to whole.}
{1231}{Jenna would like her necklace back from the kite shaman who stole it.}
{1240}{Find a Mystic Sapphire in the abandoned castle and report back to the Mayor as quickly as possible.}
{1166}{If you travel to Cattan, the Vlafa family would appreciate you keeping an eye out for their son, Lasou.}
{1167}{The Plainwicke Plantation needs help to eradicate the Merow Vortahm infestation.}
{1168}{If you happen to encounter Tasamas and Natemun Tagemie when you return to Norleigh, tell them the crisis is over, and bring anyone they hired back to Plainwicke.}
{1169}{If you decide to stop at Brookeside Plantation, Mr. Yoki would like you to inform Luroo Bobbins and Miffra Tagemie that it is safe to come home.}
{1165}{Find the hideout of I .B . Wolfe and learn the fate of the halflings he may be holding.}
{1174}{Thaddeus Mynor wants you to retrieve the S.P.A.M. Device without harming Mr. Wolfsbane.}
{1990}{A Fair Account: Recover Shareyko's tool roll from Elias Pritch at the Tarant docks, beside the ships. Pritch wants 1,000 gold, but a persuasive or charming customer may settle for 500. Return the tools to Shareyko outside the Boil.}
{1991}{A Place to Rest: Help Toby Finch leave Cedric Appleby's factory. He can wait outside the Bond residence while the house is made safe. Once both dangerous occupants are gone, check on him inside.}
{1500}{Find the stone key that opens the old tomb and bring it back to the priest. According to the latter, it is the castellan who must hold it.}
{1501}{Find a companion who can help you push the stone door of the tomb.}
{1502}{Find a way out of the valley.}
{1503}{Find 1,000 coins and give them to Leon Jourdain, the surgeon, to become his successor.}
{1504}{Find the trace of the missing woman of the castellan, so he will give me his precious pendant. Among the woman's acquaintances, the gravedigger was a close friend.}
{1505}{Find the identity of the wife's lover and reveal it to him.}
{1506}{Kill the wild beast that lives west of the mansion, on behalf of the gardener. He'll give me the gloves of Siegfried in exchange.}
